    "notes": "SUMMARY:\nMON is at a critical juncture: strong ecosystem growth and recent catalysts (Robinhood listing, RWA partnerships, privacy tech) are offset by a major token unlock scheduled for November 24, 2026 (16.8B MON, ~$410–450M value, 32.8% of circulating supply). Market sentiment is cautiously bullish on tech/adoption but polarized on supply risk. Current price at 0.02431 is up 0.79% 24h but faces volatility headwind (7d realized vol 415%, extremely high).\n\nCHAIN & MARKET OBSERVATIONS:\n- MON 7-day volatility 415.23% (annualized) with thin history warning (only 36 returns, 150+ needed); 24h vol 82.78%, 30d vol 110.47%. Extreme on 7d horizon.\n- Oracle vs pool: Chainlink 0.024344; Uniswap v4 0.024338; deviation -2.28 bps (minimal, pool trading near fair value).\n- Monad TVL $1,007.89M as of Oct 9, down 3.26% over 7 days. July peak near $1.04B; recent drawdown from Sept 21 high $1.038B to current is material.\n- DEX volume 24h: $52.69M (up 0.8% 1d). Uniswap V4 dominates at $18.59M (35% of DEX volume).\n- Top protocols stable: Aave V3 $354.2M, Euler V2 $214.6M, Risk Curators $397B combined. Aave commanding 67% of TVL.\n- Yields: USDC pools at Aave offering 1.25% (SYRUPUSDC), Accountable 10.81%, Morpho 8.08%; MON yields sparse in top 8 by TVL.\n- Pool depth sufficient at current size ($10–100 swaps): ~5 bps impact ex-fee; $1k trades 13 bps; $10k trades 85 bps.\n\nNARRATIVES FROM WEB:\n1. Token unlock dominance: Nov 24 unlock is cited as the \"most critical stress test\" (CoinMarketCap); ~$35"
